{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Israel loved Joseph.</b> From the time the Holy One, blessed be He, called his name Israel, the verses follow this practice: sometimes calling him Jacob and sometimes Israel, to indicate that what He called him — Israel — is an addition upon Jacob. And so immediately afterward: ״ויאמר ישראל אל יוסף״, and at the beginning of the parashah: ״וישב יעקב״, and so at the end of the parashah: ״ויקרע יעקב שמלותיו״." "<b>And he made him a striped tunic.</b> It was a fine garment, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 28:4): ״וכתונת תשבץ״, and it was on account of it that his brothers were jealous. From this the Rabbis of blessed memory derived: a person should never single out one son among the sons. And this tunic was the beginning of the causes, and on account of it things rolled onward to the enslavement of their bodies in Egypt, and likewise afterward, the Ten Martyrs of the Kingdom, for the body is indeed the tunic of the soul. And the expression פסים — they said in the Midrash: because it was long and covered both palms (שתי פסות) of his hands. Another interpretation: פסים — because they cast a lot (הטילו פייס) among themselves as to which of the four court-imposed deaths they would put him to, as it is said: ״ויתנכלו אותו להמיתו״. Once they sold him, they cast a lot among themselves who would bring the tunic to their father; the lot fell upon Judah — this is what he said to him: ״הכר נא״, and therefore it is said to him (Genesis 38:25): ״הכר נא למי החותמת״. And when he said to him, 'the tunic of your son,' the life of Jacob was cut off (נפסקו חייו) — therefore the lives of his sons were cut off from the world: these are Er and Onan, as it is said (Jeremiah 32:18): ״ומשלם עון אבות אל חיק בניהם אחריהם״. Another interpretation: פסים — corresponding to the four troubles that befell him: Potiphar, traders, Ishmaelites, Medanites. Another interpretation: כתונת פסים — that he transmitted to him the secret of the 22 letters, end of quote. And the intention in this is that he clothed him in the knowledge of wisdom by means of the Name of 22 letters, as he had learned from the mouth of Shem and Eber, and understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:11.769556619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}